class.description:
[method play] starts a track for a [Subtitle] and returns its ID. Each frame, the server reads the time of every track and reports which [SubtitleSegment]s start and end. The time comes from a time source, a [Callable] that returns seconds (for example [method AudioStreamPlayer.get_playback_position] or [member VideoStreamPlayer.stream_position]), or from the track's own clock, which runs in real time and can be paused and moved.
Signals are emitted on the main thread, from [method play], [method seek], [method stop] and once per frame, in this order: [signal segment_ended], [signal segment_started], [signal text_changed], then [signal track_finished]. To show subtitles, connect [signal text_changed] to a [Label] or [RichTextLabel]: it carries the text of all visible segments of a track.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
    SubtitleServer.text_changed.connect(_on_text_changed)
    SubtitleServer.track_finished.connect(_on_track_finished)
    var track_id = SubtitleServer.play(load("res://intro.srt"), $Voice.get_playback_position)
    $Voice.play()

func _on_text_changed(_track_id, text):
    $SubtitleLabel.text = text

func _on_track_finished(_track_id):
    $SubtitleLabel.text = ""
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    SubtitleServer.Singleton.TextChanged += (trackId, text) => GetNode<Label>("SubtitleLabel").Text = text;
    SubtitleServer.Singleton.TrackFinished += trackId => GetNode<Label>("SubtitleLabel").Text = "";
    var voice = GetNode<AudioStreamPlayer>("Voice");
    SubtitleServer.Play(GD.Load<Subtitle>("res://intro.srt"), new Callable(voice, AudioStreamPlayer.MethodName.GetPlaybackPosition));
    voice.Play();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] A track with a time source follows it: [method seek] is not allowed, and the track finishes when the time passes [method Subtitle.get_end_time]. If the source stops early (a player that is stopped returns [code]0.0[/code]), call [method stop]. If the object of the time source is freed, the track is canceled.
[b]Note:[/b] Segments shorter than one frame can be missed.
